WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.967 --> 00:00:02.502
Mr. Roy, a pleasure
to welcome you home.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.604
Oh, I don't recall people
shedding a tear when I left.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.874
JESSE ARMSTRONG:<i> It's a
pretty touching episode to make</i>

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:11.744 line:0%
because Brian Cox, the actor,
comes from Dundee in Scotland.

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:15.114
<i> He was the guy driving around
 places he knew from his youth</i>

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:18.084
<i> as he plays Logan,
 being a guy driving around</i>

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.486
places that he knows
from his youth, so,

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:20.886
it was very affecting
to see that.

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:24.123
This place, you look
at the old pictures

00:00:24.223 --> 00:00:25.458
and they all want you
to think it's all

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.128
so fucking simple,
but it wasn't.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.831
What they say, you know?

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:34.167
ARMSTRONG:<i> In the writer's room,
 we always knew there was</i>

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:36.636
an element of tragedy
in his early life.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.106
There it is.
What am I supposed to do?

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:43.276
I think maybe a photo.
They've said you can go in.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.546
No, thank you.
Let's go.

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:49.748
Ahh, memories.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:53.085
-Marcia, you look lovely.
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:56.689
Uh, so--
Something I wanted to ask you...

00:00:57.256 --> 00:00:59.092
ARMSTRONG:<i> Marcia,
 she doesn't come from the same</i>

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:01.527
cultural background
as the rest of the characters,

00:01:01.627 --> 00:01:03.128
